  "status": "draft",
  "notes": "Journey Through Middle-Earth (S5 draft). One day on dayOfYear 78 (sunrise 6.09, sunset 17.91, the sun key fades out by 18.32 and the moon key comes in from 18.3 to 18.85, full night 19.37; waxing moon ≈ 70 % lit, 57–62° up from 18:00). Beats alternate hold / move; durations are cumulative. Camera keys reference landmark bookmarks or QA shots (+ `set` overrides) and never edit them (five bookmarks are lock-v1 sentinels). The hold azimuths run as one journey heading (consecutive holds ≤ ~110° apart, moves turn < 30°/s): south of the road through Eriador (the morning sun from the right), west of the Misty Mountains for Rivendell and Moria, then swinging back through south to the north-east over Rohan and the Anduin (Lórien 200, Isengard 130, Helm's Deep 40, Edoras 60, the Argonath 33, the Black Gate 342) and back counter-clockwise west of the Anduin round Gondor (Henneth Annûn 290 from over the river, Minas Tirith 185 from the south with Osgiliath and the route head in frame, Minas Morgul 195, Mount Doom 166): the camera stays over the river lands, never over the Ephel Dúath (a Minas Tirith key east of the city put the approach over the mountains: the head hidden, the ash deck crossed). Rauros is passed inside the move to the Black Gate (a pass caption while the head goes by). Moves: apexEl 26 (a higher apex swung the view up and down faster than 30°/s), per-move rho / apexEl where a move dips under the clearance margin, jerks, loses the head or shows the board's edge (a low apex where both holds look at the horizon keeps the frame top in the sky). Minas Tirith is at blue hour (Mindolluin shades it all afternoon); Minas Morgul at 18.85–18.95 under the rising moon (the vale's luma 23 at 18.75 → 35 at 18.95) (the moon key only comes in between sun −4° and −11°, 18.3 → 18.85). Compiled by src/tour/compile.ts; checked by tools/check/film.ts (pnpm check).",
